  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;If <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the inverse function of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>g</mi> <mo>′</mo> </msup> <mfenced> <mn>4</mn> </mfenced></mrow> </math> is equal to",
